        "symbol": "I",
        "family": "forms",
        "short": "The induced metric: lengths, angles, areas on the surface.",
        "definition": "The restriction of the ambient inner product to tangent vectors, I(v,w)=⟨dx(v),dx(w)⟩, written in coordinates as E du²+2F du dv+G dv². It encodes all intrinsic measurements.",
        "intuition": "What a flat creature living in the surface can measure without ever leaving it: distances along curves, angles between them, and patch areas.",
        "watch": "I alone does not determine how the surface sits in space — many embeddings (plane vs. cylinder) share the same I."
