        "definition": "A primal-dual feasible pair is optimal iff, for each variable, either it is zero or its associated dual constraint is tight, and symmetrically for each constraint and its dual variable.",
        "intuition": "It is the equality case of weak duality made local: zero total slack forces each product term to vanish, linking which constraints bind to which variables are active.",
        "watch": "It characterizes optimality only for an already-feasible pair; it is not a feasibility test, and it presumes the strong-duality setting where the optima coincide."
