        "family": "bridge",
        "short": "For every ε, finitely many ε-balls cover the space.",
        "definition": "A space is totally bounded if for each ε > 0 it can be covered by finitely many balls of radius ε.",
        "intuition": "The space has finite 'ε-resolution' at every scale — equivalently, every sequence has a Cauchy subsequence. It controls width, not whether limits exist.",
        "watch": "Totally bounded does not imply complete: the open interval (0,1) is totally bounded yet missing its endpoints. The two notions are independent ingredients."
