        "symbol": "H≅H*",
        "family": "spaces",
        "short": "Every bounded functional is ⟨·,y⟩ for a unique y.",
        "definition": "For each bounded linear functional φ on H there is a unique y ∈ H with φ(x) = ⟨x,y⟩ for all x, and ‖φ‖ = ‖y‖; this identifies H with its dual H*.",
        "intuition": "A Hilbert space is its own dual — measuring a vector against functionals is the same as taking inner products with vectors.",
        "watch": "The map y ↦ ⟨·,y⟩ is conjugate-linear, so H ≅ H* is an antilinear (not linear) isometric isomorphism. Completeness is essential."
