        "definition": "The adjoint of a bounded T is the unique bounded operator T* satisfying ⟨Tx,y⟩ = ⟨x,T*y⟩ for all x,y; it exists by Riesz and obeys ‖T*‖ = ‖T‖, T** = T.",
        "intuition": "The abstract conjugate-transpose: it moves an operator across the inner product. The C*-identity ‖T*T‖ = ‖T‖² makes B(H) a C*-algebra.",
        "watch": "Existence of T* relies on the Riesz theorem, hence on completeness; on a mere inner product space the adjoint can fail to exist."
