        "family": "operators",
        "short": "Commutes with its adjoint: TT* = T*T.",
        "definition": "A bounded operator with TT* = T*T. Self-adjoint, unitary, and skew-adjoint operators are all special cases.",
        "intuition": "Commuting with its adjoint is exactly the condition that makes an operator diagonalizable by a spectral measure — the dividing line for clean spectral theory.",
        "watch": "Normality is equivalent to ‖Tx‖ = ‖T*x‖ for all x. It is strictly weaker than self-adjoint and strictly weaker than unitary."
