        "family": "operators",
        "short": "Invertible isometry: U*U = UU* = I.",
        "definition": "A bounded operator with U*U = UU* = I; equivalently a surjective isometry, U preserves the inner product ⟨Ux,Uy⟩ = ⟨x,y⟩ and maps H onto H.",
        "intuition": "The rigid symmetries of Hilbert space — they preserve all lengths and angles and are perfectly invertible, the operator analogue of a unit-modulus complex number.",
