          "NTT-friendly primes like p = 998244353 (= 119·2^23 + 1) used in competitive programming and crypto",
          "Reed-Solomon and BCH codes define codewords as polynomials vanishing at consecutive roots of unity",
          "Multiplicative group of a finite field F_q is cyclic of order q-1 — its generators are primitive (q-1)-th roots of unity"
