    "applications": "Computing Betti numbers and detecting holes/handles of manifolds analytically; electromagnetism (Maxwell's equations are dF=0 and d*F=J, with magnetic monopole charge and Aharonov-Bohm phases living in H^2 and H^1); fluid dynamics and the Helmholtz decomposition of vector fields; obstruction theory for \"potential exists\" questions (conservative fields, exact differentials in thermodynamics). It underlies Chern-Weil theory, where curvature forms of a connection represent characteristic classes (Chern, Pontryagin, Euler) in de Rham cohomology, and the Gauss-Bonnet and Atiyah-Singer index theorems express topological integers as integrals of curvature. In data analysis the Hodge Laplacian and discrete exterior calculus port these ideas to graphs and meshes for ranking, flow decomposition, and topological signal processing.",
