          "decidable coefficient rings by contrast: R (Tarski, real closed fields) and C (Nullstellensatz / ACF) both have decidable existential theories",
          "open and recent: Hilbert's 10th over Q is still open (Koenigsmann's and Poonen's work on defining Z in Q is the main attack); over rings of integers of arbitrary number fields it was proved undecidable in 2024 by Koymans-Pagano, with related work of Alpoege-Bhargava-Ho-Shnidman, replacing earlier results conditional on BSD/Shafarevich-Tate-type conjectures"
