        "name": "Continuous time, Lyapunov functions and control",
        "gist": "Taking the step size to zero turns momentum methods into second-order ODEs, where the rate is a one-line energy computation and the mysterious coefficient schedules become damping laws. The same dynamical view lets control theory certify and design algorithms.",
