          "finite = integral + finite type: k[t^2,t^3] subset k[t] is finite (t^2 - (t^2) = 0), while k[x] subset k[x,1/x] is not integral (1/x satisfies no monic equation)",
          "Artin-Tate lemma and Eakin-Nagata: finiteness transfers down to subrings, which is how Noether's finiteness theorem for invariants is proved",
