        "name": "Closed sets, the V-I correspondence, and the distinguished basis",
        "gist": "Closed means \"common zero locus of some polynomials\"; V and I form an inclusion-reversing Galois connection whose two closure operators are Zariski closure and (over an algebraically closed field, by the Nullstellensatz) radical. The sets D(f) = {f != 0} form a basis, and each is itself affine with coordinate ring the localization k[X]_f.",
