          "P^1(C) is the Riemann sphere; P^2(R) is a closed nonorientable surface with chi = 1, and RP^n is orientable iff n is odd",
          "Weighted projective space P(a_0..a_n), the quotient by t.(x_i) = (t^(a_i) x_i): still complete, but singular in general — a first hint that Proj is the right general construction"
