          "Chow's theorem: a closed analytic subset of P^n(C) is algebraic; with GAGA, coherent-sheaf theory on projective varieties is the same analytically and algebraically",
          "Complete does not mean projective: Hironaka's smooth complete non-projective 3-fold. But every complete curve, and every smooth complete surface (Zariski), is projective"
