          "Spec k[x] with k algebraically closed: closed points (x - a) <-> a in k, plus (0). Spec R[x] instead has (0), (x - a) for a in R, and (x^2 + bx + c) with b^2 - 4c < 0",
          "Spec Z[x] has dimension 2: (0), the (p), the (f) with f irreducible, and maximal ideals (p, f) with f irreducible mod p",
          "quasi-compactness is Bezout-trivial: Spec A = union of D(f_i) means 1 lies in the ideal generated by the f_i, hence in one generated by finitely many of them"
