          "characteristic p group schemes μ_p = Spec F_p[x]/((x-1)^p) and α_p = Spec F_p[x]/(x^p) are nonreduced and nontrivial; by Cartier's theorem, group schemes of finite type over a field of characteristic 0 are always reduced, so these have no char-0 analogue",
          "moduli: Mumford's classical example gives an irreducible component of the Hilbert scheme of smooth degree-14 genus-24 space curves in P^3 that is everywhere non-reduced — the obstruction theory sits in the nilpotents"
