          "for k algebraically closed and A a finitely generated reduced k-algebra, MaxSpec A is the classical affine variety (weak Nullstellensatz via Zariski's lemma) and Spec A adds exactly one generic point per irreducible closed subset",
          "a K-point for a field K is a point x together with an embedding κ(x) -> K; geometric points take K algebraically closed",
