          "Semilinear waves u_tt - Δu = |u|^p: the Strauss exponent p_0(n), the positive root of (n-1)p^2 - (n+1)p - 2 = 0, separates small-data global existence (p > p_0) from finite-time blow-up (p <= p_0); settled for this model problem, still active on manifolds and with variable coefficients",
