        "name": "Variational characterization and eigenvalue estimates",
        "gist": "Eigenvalues are critical values of the Rayleigh quotient, which converts spectral questions into minimization and thereby yields bounds, monotonicity and asymptotics without solving anything. The min-max principle is the workhorse: it gives comparison theorems, domain monotonicity, and the numerical convergence theory of Rayleigh–Ritz and finite elements.",
