          "hat f(xi) = (2 pi)^{-n/2} int f e^{-i x.xi} dx (symmetric / quantum mechanics): unitary and inversion-symmetric, but convolution acquires a factor (2 pi)^{n/2}.",
          "hat f(xi) = int f e^{-i x.xi} dx (Hormander, PDE): hat{d_j f} = i xi_j hat f is clean, but inversion and Plancherel carry (2 pi)^{-n}.",
          "Conversion: all conventions are related by a dilation xi |-> c xi plus an overall constant, using hat{f(lambda .)}(xi) = lambda^{-n} hat f(xi/lambda); Mathematica parametrizes the whole family by FourierParameters {a,b}.",
          "Probabilists' characteristic function phi_X(t) = E e^{i t.X} equals hat mu(-t/(2 pi)) in the e^{-2 pi i x.xi} convention."
