          "L^2 multipliers are exactly L^inf with ||T||_{L^2 -> L^2} = ||m||_inf (Plancherel); L^1 multipliers are exactly convolutions with finite measures",
          "Hormander-Mikhlin theorem: symbol bounds |D^a m(xi)| <= C |xi|^{-|a|} for |a| <= floor(n/2)+1 give L^p boundedness, 1 < p < inf",
