          "Marcinkiewicz interpolation between (1, weak 1) and (2,2), then duality against the transposed kernel for p>2",
          "The good-lambda inequality |{T*f > 2L, Mf <= gL}| <= C g |{T*f > L}| and the Fefferman-Stein sharp maximal function as an alternative route to L^p",
          "Modern replacement: Lerner's sparse domination, |<Tf,g>| <= C sum_{Q in S} avg_Q|f| avg_Q|g| |Q| over a sparse family S"
