          "Chetaev's theorem applied to x' = x^3 + xy^2 type fields with V = x^2 - y^2 on the cone |x| > |y|, proving instability where linearization is silent",
          "The radial-unboundedness counterexample V = x1^2/(1+x1^2) + x2^2: Vdot < 0 everywhere but sublevel sets are unbounded strips and trajectories can escape along them",
