      {
        "name": "Enriched Yoneda, weighted limits and Cauchy completion",
        "gist": "Enriched category theory is not a cosmetic rewrite: ordinary conical limits are too weak, and the right notion is a limit weighted by a V-functor, with the enriched Yoneda lemma and ends/coends as the basic tools.",
        "examples": [
          "Enriched Yoneda lemma over a cosmos (complete, cocomplete, symmetric monoidal closed): [C,V](C(A,−),F) ≅ F A, with weak form V-Nat(C(A,−),F) ≅ V(I, F A)",
          "Weighted (indexed) limits lim^W F characterized by D(d, lim^W F) ≅ [C,V](W, D(d,F−)); for V = Set they reduce to conical limits over the category of elements of W, but not in general",
          "Tensors and cotensors (copowers and powers): a V-category is complete iff it admits conical limits and cotensors — the standard reduction in Kelly's book",
          "Ends and coends: the V-natural transformation object as an end ∫_A D(F A, G A); coend calculus as the computational engine (Day convolution, Kan extensions, geometric realization)",
          "Cauchy completion in the enriched sense: idempotent splitting for V = Set, finitely generated projective modules and Morita equivalence for V = Ab, and the usual metric completion for symmetric spaces when V = [0,∞]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "Tensor categories, Tannakian reconstruction and TQFT",
        "gist": "Rigid abelian monoidal categories with a fiber functor can be reconstructed as representation categories, and symmetric monoidal functors out of cobordism categories are exactly topological field theories — two of the deepest payoffs of the monoidal viewpoint.",
        "examples": [
          "Tannaka: for a compact group G, G is isomorphic to the group of UNITARY monoidal natural automorphisms of the forgetful functor Rep(G) → Hilb (dropping unitarity yields the complexification); neutral Tannakian categories over k with an exact faithful fiber functor are Rep of an affine group scheme (Saavedra, Deligne-Milne)",
          "Deligne (2002): over an algebraically closed field of characteristic 0, a rigid symmetric monoidal abelian k-linear category with End(1) = k and moderate growth (lengths of X^{⊗n} at most exponential, equivalently every object killed by some Schur functor) is Rep of an affine SUPERgroup scheme; the naive characteristic-p analogue is false and the p-adic/positive-characteristic classification is active research",
          "Fusion categories (semisimple, rigid, finitely many simples, simple unit) and modular tensor categories; Ocneanu rigidity (Etingof-Nikshych-Ostrik): over an algebraically closed field of characteristic 0 only finitely many fusion categories share a given fusion ring",
          "Atiyah's axioms: an n-dimensional TQFT is a symmetric monoidal functor (Cob_n, ⊔) → (Vect_k, ⊗); the 2-dimensional oriented case is classified by commutative Frobenius algebras; Reshetikhin-Turaev builds (2+1)-dimensional theories from modular categories",
          "Cobordism hypothesis (Baez-Dolan conjecture, proof strategy given by Lurie): framed fully extended n-dimensional TQFTs valued in a symmetric monoidal (∞,n)-category correspond to its fully dualizable objects — widely accepted, with complete written proofs still being assembled in the literature"
        ]
      }
