          "Morita theory: R-Mod equivalent to S-Mod iff S = End_R(P) for a finitely generated projective generator P; Morita invariants include the center, K-theory and the lattice of two-sided ideals, but not commutativity",
          "Gabriel-Popescu: every Grothendieck category is a left-exact localization of a module category — Hom(U,-) is fully faithful with an exact left adjoint, for U a generator, R = End(U)",
