          "Z is integrally closed in Q, so a rational algebraic integer is an ordinary integer (rational root theorem)",
          "Zbar, the ring of all algebraic integers in C: integrally closed, dimension 1, a Bezout domain, but not Noetherian (the chain (2^{1/2}) < (2^{1/4}) < (2^{1/8}) < ... never stabilizes)",
