          "Non-maximal orders fail worse: Z[sqrt(-3)] is not integrally closed and 4 = 2*2 = (1+sqrt(-3))(1-sqrt(-3)), while the maximal order Z[(1+sqrt(-3))/2] is a PID",
          "Class number one for imaginary quadratic fields occurs exactly nine times: d = -1,-2,-3,-7,-11,-19,-43,-67,-163 (Heegner–Baker–Stark); for real quadratic fields infinitude of h = 1 is conjectured and open",
