          "Localization: (O_K)_P is a DVR with valuation ord_P; any localization S^{-1}R of a Dedekind domain is Dedekind (or a field)",
          "Non-examples pinning down each axiom: Z[sqrt(-3)] (not integrally closed), k[x,y] (dimension 2), the ring of all algebraic integers (integrally closed, dimension 1, but not Noetherian — a Bezout domain)",
          "Krull–Akizuki: for A Noetherian of dimension 1 with Frac(A) = K and L/K finite, any ring between A and L is Noetherian of dimension <= 1, so the integral closure is Dedekind — though module-finiteness over A can fail without separability or excellence hypotheses"
